WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.402
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.570
-Thanks for having me.
-Fresh off the VMAs.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.237
You performed last night.
You closed out the show.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:07.373
-Yeah. Does anyone
have a Band-id?

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:11.110
I like, pulled giant piece of
my guitar out of my hand.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.478
-Just now?
-Yeah.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.013
But it's been --
Well, I did it last night.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:16.048
But it won't stop bleeding,
so I just keep wiping it

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:17.349
on the inside of my pant.

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.551
Maybe I'll just keep my hand
in my pants.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.353
-That's cool.
Yeah, that looks very natural.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.188
Unfortunately,
they all know why.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.758
-Okay.
-We'll get you a Band-Aid.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.492
You know, I'm actually
genuinely curious

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.795
how long it takes to get
a Band-Aid during an interview.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.596
We'll see if we can even
make it in time.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.165
But you mentioned that you got
a piece of your guitar.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.469
I always get nervous when people
try to smash guitars.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.504
Were you nervous
that you weren't gonna be able

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.141
to effectively smash it?
You did a great job.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.042
-Well, that was never
part of the plan.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.546
I kind of did it out of, um...

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.448
There could be a documentary
about everything that happened

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.351
backstage at the VMAs
last night.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.620
-A documentary about how it went
exactly according to plan?

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.288
-Yeah, yeah.
I wasn't supposed to

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.190
close out the show.
-Look at this.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.293
-Oh, my God. Thank you so much.
-Look how fast it came.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.061
You weren't supposed to
close out the show?

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.529
-No.
-Seems to me, like,

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.098
at award shows there's usually
a pretty hard locked-in list.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.200
-Yeah, it was -- Yeah.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.236
-So, they came to you
and said, "Change of plans.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.937
You're going to close"?
-I was in my set piece.

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:14.607
I was in the grave.
If you watch the performance,

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.375
I start out in a grave.
And i got --

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.512
In the middle of the show,
they took me out of the grave,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.081
and it -- dude,
story for another day.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.016
-That is -- Well, I don't know.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.185
Seems like this is
a pretty good place for it.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:28.588
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.057
I do like the idea
of somebody being, like,

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.326
"Somebody has to go tell
Machine Gun he's not on."

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.828
It's like, "He's
already in the grave."

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.396
-"Yeah, I was in the --
For real.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.532
-So, were you fully covered,
so somebody had to come over

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.800
and, like,
knock-knock on the grave?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.968
-No, the grave
was an open grave.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.437
-Did you then, when it was
all over, it went well?

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:47.406
You won.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:50.276
-You got an award presented
to you on television.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.877
Did you then go out
later in the night?

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.279
Be honest.
-I did.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.982
I ran into Pete last night.
-Yeah, Pete did a concert --

00:01:55.982 --> 00:02:00.486
a stand-up comedy show for 9/11
at Madison Square Garden.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:01.754
So, you went out,
you saw
your friend Pete.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.923
-I saw Pete, and
I saw Chappelle.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.160
-Had you met Chappelle before?
-Well, funny story.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.228
That was the first time
me, Pete, and Dave

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:13.132
have been in a room
since Dave flew me and Pete

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.101
out to his house to -- to smoke.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:17.337
-To -- To smoke weed?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.006
-And then he sent us back
'cause I had a show.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.742
He found out Pete was going
to Ohio for my show.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.845
Christmas show.
And he was like, "Oh,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.213
you guys just got to come down
and hang out."

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.482
I'm like, "Oh, you're
like five hours away, driving."

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.050
He's like, "No worries.
There's a jet there

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.052
waiting for you.
You guys have to get on it."

00:02:34.052 --> 00:02:36.089
And we got on. We landed.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.024
He forgot it was
his mom's 81st birthday.

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:41.227
-Uh-huh.
-As we all do.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.694
-Right, well, if you're
the kind of person

00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:44.931
who flies people in for weed,
you tend to forget dates.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.398
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:48.934
And so we went --
So, he picks us up.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.137
We go there.
And then --

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:54.373
I don't know
if I can say all this.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:58.644
It was just like -- It was --
I mean, it was

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:02.081
the most legendary --
it certified Dave Chappelle

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.616
as, like, the ultimate
rock star, to me.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.452
-And is this a photo from then?
-No, this is --

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.355
-I was like, "This is not
the photo I expected,

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.656
based on what you just said."

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.925
-No, that was actually
from a couple days ago.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.894
Pete flew in.
I wrote and directed this movie

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:17.363
with a friend of mine, Mod Sun,

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.798
and he came in to do a cameo
on the last day.

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:21.467
And he was like,
"We should have breakfast."

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.403
And I got to breakfast.
And we were looking at the menu

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:27.640
and both of us saw this drink.
And we were --

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:31.310
You know, we're kind of looking
at the name of it.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.378
And we were like,
"It looks so good,

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:34.814
but, like, I don't want to be
the one to order it."

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.315
So we both looked at the waiter,
and we're like,

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.983
"Can we get two Beach Boys,
please?"

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:40.052
[ Laughter ]
-The Beach Boys!

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.787
-It's so funny.
-You guys are

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.389
the new Beach Boys.
I love it.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.824
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.726
So you went -- I just want to
get the timeline right.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.794
You were doing a show in Ohio,

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:50.229
and instead of
driving five hours,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.066
Chappelle jets you to his place.
-We fly back.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.302
-How long are you there?
-We do, like, a solid

00:03:56.302 --> 00:04:00.106
Mom's 81st birthday --
-So, you went to the party?

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.541
-Yeah, which it was a party.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.610
81-year-olds go hard.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.978
-Absolutely, they do.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:08.347
-Did that, two hours.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.751
Chappelle has different
man caves around the town.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:15.521
So we stopped in there.
Talib Kweli was in one.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:19.291
We went to another place.
It was the most random night.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:23.830
We end up at his house.
His wife was, like, furious

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.299
that we were still there, like,
"Get these idiots out of here."

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.000
So he's like, "Alright, you guys
got to get back on the plane."

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.802
So, we get on the plane,
go, we do the concert.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.971
And then me, Pete,
and my daughter decide

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:34.206
to do an eight-hour road trip
to New York

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.008
to go to his mom's house,
and we spent Christmas

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.776
at his mom's house.
-That's fantastic.

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:40.546
Well turned around.
Your daughter is 12 years old?

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:41.847
-Mm-hmm.
-And does she ever go

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.182
to your shows?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.050
-Does she enjoy?
-Yeah, for sure.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.586
-Great.
-She's a concert kid.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.621
-And she can stay up late
and do that whole thing?

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.257
I guess, 12, I would imagine,
at this point, yeah.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.825
-She looks at me
like I'm a loser.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.761
I'm like, "Alright,
it's 1:00 a.m.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.029
I'm gonna tap out."
She's like, "Pbht, dork."

00:04:57.029 --> 00:05:00.699
-I have a quick -- I have
a tattoo question.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:02.235
I know you have a lot.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.136
Maybe something that you
and Pete connected on.

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.305
One thing that he's talked about
on the show is, like,

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.041
sometimes you have one
that you end up

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.675
maybe regretting over time.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:13.245
You've gotten all your album
titles tattooed on yourself.

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:17.149
Does that then put a higher
burden of pressure on the title

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:19.051
when you're coming up with it,
knowing that you're gonna

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.320
get it inked on?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.957
-It puts pressure on
how well the album does.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.959
No one wants to put the flop
on their body.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.327
-Sure.
I didn't think about that.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.763
-It's done me well so far.
It progressively

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.298
has gotten better,
every release.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:35.101
I'm just worried, if it
turns into a Jay-Z situation,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:38.404
where I have like 13 albums
and then I end up having to be

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.939
like, "I ran out of space.
I guess

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.308
I'm doing it right here
on my nose."

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.676
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-Or, like, my eye.

00:05:44.676 --> 00:05:46.011
I have to sacrifice an eyebrow
and just put --

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.280
-Yeah, you can't be
that prolific.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.014
You got to, like, tap the brakes
a little bit.

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:53.018
-Like, lie that
Seth Meyers' kitchen...

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:55.721
-We would love to do
one of your live albums.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.055
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.055 --> 00:06:00.793
Hey, this is really cool.
You wrote this graphic novel.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:04.163
You got a bunch of
different really great artists

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.765
to work on it.
-Yes.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.232
-I've only done it the one time.

00:06:07.232 --> 00:06:10.036
Bill Hader and I wrote
a comic book a long time ago.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:13.105
The most exciting thing for me
was when the art comes back.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:16.041
Was that just so thrilling?
-Yes.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.510
Um, uh...
[ Sighs ]

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.813
Yes, and, like,
it was really cool

00:06:21.813 --> 00:06:26.552
being able to reach out
to certain artists that I --

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.354
like, I love the way
that the art looks

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.755
in "Ice Cream Man."
-Yeah.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:32.357
-And we were able to get
certain people

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:34.927
that I was fans of
to contribute to this.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:38.464
I'm more of
a cerebral comic reader.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.933
Like, I love graphic novels
that have --

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:44.336
that take you on, like,
really intricate journey.

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:45.605
I like "Sandman."

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.606
We were talking about "Sandman"
backstage.

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:51.310
So I'm hoping to turn this
into something that becomes

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.978
a world, kind of like --

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:59.351
I love how Disney World
is such a fantasy, like, place

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:01.220
that is --
you know, you can go to.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.388
-This does not strike me
to be like Disney World.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.289
-This is a little bit opposite
of Disney World.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:05.791
-I don't want to show
some of these pictures,

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:08.026
but it's very not-Disney World.

00:07:08.026 --> 00:07:09.695
-The audience
doesn't have to see,

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:13.966
but these are things
we don't show the television.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.201
-No, we don't
show the television this.

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:16.535
Here, I'll just give a line.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.638
"The man killed when I was 17."

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.806
-Ah.
-That's my favorite ride.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.975
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.244
-At Disney World.
It's so great.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.713
You start on, like --
you're on a roller coaster,

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:28.881
and on the way up, it's like,

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.816
"Tick, tick, tick, tick,
tick, tick, thump!"

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.085
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.686
-And then everyone
on the roller coaster

00:07:34.686 --> 00:07:37.123
is like, "Wait, what was that?"
and then you just hear sirens.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:39.024
-And the police come
and arrest everybody.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:40.493
Like, "Well,
you just culled somebody.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:43.228
You'll have to go to jail.
You're a lifer."

00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:47.199
-So, you -- you grew up --
I know, Cleveland.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:48.768
-Mm-hmm.
-Worked in a mall.

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:51.437
And this was when you were
also -- you had mixtapes.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.771
You were doing mixtapes.
-Yeah.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:54.873
-That's a very cool thing
to be doing.

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.341
What were the stores
you were working in,

00:07:56.341 --> 00:07:59.011
at the mall, at the time?
-I worked in an airbrush store

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.880
for many year.
-What were people getting

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.514
airbrushed. back in the day,
when you were there?

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:08.854
-A lot of "RIPs",
and a lot of "free."

00:08:08.854 --> 00:08:10.990
-Okay.
-Whoever. "Free Chris."

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.691
-Okay.
-You know?

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:15.294
-When someone got arrested,
that was when a lot of money

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:17.095
came into the shop.
-Interesting.

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:20.766
So that would be
a bad time for the Chrises,

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.968
but a good time
for the airbrush.

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:24.670
-There wasn't a person
that came in

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.972
that I wouldn't rap for.
Anybody that came in,

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:29.975
I was, "Enjoy this T-shirt.
Now, also,

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:32.778
I'm going to rap for you
for the next three minutes."

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.814
-Great.
So, not "Here's a mixtape."

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.248
You were like, "I'm gonna
do it face-to-face.

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:38.784
-I would also like
to charge you 5 extra dollars

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.185
to leave with my mixtape."

00:08:40.185 --> 00:08:42.588
-Wow. What was the sort of
hit rate you had?

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.723
How many people were actually
buying the mixtape?

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:47.259
-You'd be surprised at how many
people in Cleveland

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:49.529
come up to me now,
when I'm walking around,

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.063
that are like, "Dude,
I remember you

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.431
when you used to rap
in the airbrush shop."

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:55.468
-Really?!
-'Cause Tower City is

00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:57.603
the middle point of Cleveland
between East and West Side.

00:08:57.603 --> 00:09:01.274
All the trains -- there's
one train station in the middle.

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:03.309
So all the trains would come up,

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:05.477
and everyone would come up
in between their stops

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:06.912
and, like, after school
and everything.

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:08.280
And so anyone that was --

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.448
And the movie theater
was right there.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.916
When "You Got Served"
was in theaters,

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:12.918
and everyone came out,
I was just in the hallway

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:16.288
the whole time, like,
[Imitating drumrolls]

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:18.323
[ Laughter ]
-So, you would just wait

00:09:18.323 --> 00:09:19.692
for people
to come out of a movie,

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:21.059
'cause you thought if they
were at that movie --

00:09:21.059 --> 00:09:22.995
-The movie theater was
right next to the airbrush.

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:25.664
-And you would just, like, rap?
And now how many people --

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:27.600
When people say,
"I remember you rapping,"

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.768
are they saying,
"I bought your mixtape"?

00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:31.237
Or do you think now they regret
that they --

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:34.006
-No, a lot of people bought.

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:36.775
Like, I was -- That was
how people heard.

00:09:36.775 --> 00:09:38.076
That was how the labels
heard about me,

00:09:38.076 --> 00:09:41.847
because I was a really big
